<item>
  <title>Welcome — what this blog is for</title>
  <link>https://terryfxh.github.io/math-notes/posts/welcome/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p>This blog is where I work mathematics out in the open. The goal is a small archive of <strong>self-contained, correct notes</strong> — results derived from first principles, papers digested into something I’d actually want to re-read, and numerical methods tested with code you can run yourself.</p>
<section id="how-posts-are-organized" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="how-posts-are-organized">How posts are organized</h2>
<p>Each post belongs to one of a few pillars:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pure</strong> — analysis, algebra, topology, number theory</li>
<li><strong>Applied</strong> — numerical methods, optimization, probability, PDEs</li>
<li><strong>Meta</strong> — paper reviews, study notes, problem sets</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="a-standing-promise" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="a-standing-promise">A standing promise</h2>
<p>Every claim here is proved, cited, or explicitly flagged as intuition. When I get something wrong, I fix it — corrections are welcome via the repo’s issues.</p>
<p>Next up: the <a href="../spectral-theorem/">Spectral Theorem note</a> shows the formatting these posts use — theorems, proofs, citations, and runnable code.</p>


<!-- -->

</section>

